# The memory paid back (content plan phase 0, T25): chip headroom in play and
# the AROS boot margin. The chopper's frames, the BOBs and the bands are floppy
# files, not program data, and the chopper's sprite DMA reads four small
# blocks (per copper buffer and rotor phase) the blitter refills when the
# pose changes, not two resident sets of every frame.
# - bootvbl: when the first picture came up, in CIA-A TOD counts (main.c
#   bootReady). The harness waits 3000 frames from power-on for it; TOD trails
#   that count by the ROM's start-up (AROS 102 frames, KS 3.1 138, KS 1.3 333).
#   AROS, the slowest loader (~10 frames a KB of program), must show its first
#   picture by harness frame 2700 or so: bootvbl 2590 or less. (The other ROMs
#   load faster and pass with room.)
# - songs on the floppy (T26): the three songs (33 KB) are not program data either,
#   so AROS shows its first picture ~140 frames sooner (2464 -> 2324 measured, the
#   program loads ~4.4 frames a KB there): bootvbl 2350 or less (was 2590).
# - chip: free chip RAM never below 96 KB in play on any profile (the game's
#   floor is 64, SPEC 2: this keeps 32 KB of it for the world-arena work).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
expect-serial "bootvbl=([0-9]{1,3}|1[0-9]{3}|2[0-2][0-9]{2}|23[0-4][0-9]|2350)\b"
press fire 2
wait 125
press up 30
press left 170
wait 60
press down 70
expect-serial "landed x=2334"
wait 60
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-min-chip-free 96
